Z||000000||1986 Fiero||05-21-2001||12:06 PM||||I am the guy that had that fiero with front end damage for sale..well i decided to keep the car my father is helping me fix it...I am cleaning the interor the car from sitting for two years got some water inside the car and now it has a very bad sickning smell...I am going to take the seats out does anyone know what would work good to clean the inside with to hopefully get red of that smell?<BR>                Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-21-2001||12:26 PM||||I used Resolve Carpet cleaner on mine, i did it a few times then i used fabreese on the seats and stuff... worked great||||reg||1
Z||000002||RacinRob||05-21-2001||01:01 PM||||I've used a steam cleaner that I rented from a store and that worked great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||05-21-2001||01:06 PM||||If you have a Shop Vac and tools, do this...<P>Get a bucket of hot, soapy water, a sponge and a scrub brush. Take out the seats, use the sponge to wet the carpet (don't soak it), then use the scrub brush to work up a foam. Then use the Shop Vac to suck the water from the carpet. Do the same with the seats and door panels (don't soak these either).<P>Then park the car out in the sun with the windows down. <P>Takes about an hour or two and it works wonders.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-21-2001||01:52 PM||||what kinda sicking smell is it? maybe you got a dead mouse inside one of the seats, or up under the working parts of the cars somewhere.||||reg||1
